From 7026c2896718d38bb8625b1dc33e825824297514 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Viren070 <viren070@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:45:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ass_font: let threads share fonts

FreeType lets one thread at a time use a face, so each font has a lock
for its faces. Faces are added under the font selector's lock, which
FT_Library needs too, and published with an atomic count. Glyph indices
are cached per face so that the shaper's lookups take no lock.
